    "field": "Agricultural water management",
    "problem": "Existing methods for estimating irrigation water withdrawals, such as FAO surveys and Global Models, suffer from excessive complexity and data uncertainty, which obscures the dominant role of irrigated areas and prevents a transparent assessment of their reliability for water security policy.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a parsimonious method using linear regression with uncertainty and sensitivity analysis to estimate irrigation water withdrawals as a function of irrigated areas, providing a robust and transparent alternative to complex Global Models.",
    "task": "The task is to estimate global irrigation water withdrawals using a parsimonious model based on irrigated areas, demonstrating it is as effective and more transparent than complex Global Models and survey-based approaches.",
